"assessment_outcome": "temporarily_unfit",
"explanation": "The patient has experienced two blackouts of undetermined nature separated by at least 24 hours. According to the supplied guideline evidence, a person should not drive for 10 years following two or more such blackouts. Although the patient reports exactly ten event-free years since the last event, the mechanism remains undetermined after investigation, and the diagnosis excludes syncope, seizure, or another condition. This establishes an established restriction preventing driving pending further investigation or stabilization of the cause. The absence of verified facts regarding a confirmed diagnosis (e.g., syncope) means the conditional standard cannot be met; therefore, the outcome is temporary unfitness rather than a conditional permission.",
"criterion_checks": [
{
"module": "blackout",
"passage_id": "PASS-c2389eae9eca5bb96ceb386b",
"fact_fields": ["blackout.occurred", "blackout.episodes_separated_by_24h_count", "blackout.mechanism_status"],
"licence_pathway": "both",
"finding": "established_restriction",
"conclusion": "The patient has two blackouts of undetermined nature separated by 24 hours, and the mechanism is undetermined. Guideline AFTD2022-BLK-COM-005 states that a person should not drive for 10 years following two or more blackouts of undetermined nature separated by a 24-hour period."
},
{
"module": "blackout",
"passage_id": "PASS-c2389eae9eca5bb96ceb386b",
